Jira IMAC-1262 – Code Update Description

Title: POC: Replicate IMAC Infrastructure Governance Policy Check Using GitHub Actions

Description

Created a standalone GitHub Actions workflow (infra-policy-check.yml) to replicate the existing Jenkins infra_policy_check.sh governance process. The workflow retrieves IMAC project and environment configuration from DynamoDB, dynamically generates OPA tagging data, and evaluates Terraform plans against the existing infrastructure tagging policies.

The workflow runs on the IMAC self-hosted GitHub Actions runner and supports automatic execution on pushes to the main branch, as well as manual execution for testing.

Changes Implemented

Created .github/workflows/infra-policy-check.yml as a separate governance workflow without modifying the existing Terraform plan workflow.

Configured automatic execution on pushes to main and manual execution through workflow_dispatch.

Added validation for required tools, including AWS CLI, Terraform, jq, OPA, and Git.

Implemented Terraform plan retrieval from S3 and conversion to JSON for OPA evaluation.

Integrated the existing CDO/imac-policies repository to retrieve infrastructure governance policies.

Added DynamoDB integration to retrieve IMAC_CONFIG from dev-ImacConfigTable using the runner's AWS credentials.

Implemented dynamic generation of opa/policies/data.json containing the configured IMAC projects and environments.

Added OPA policy evaluation using the cdo/terraform/required_default_tagging/deny decision path.

Configured the workflow to fail when the Terraform plan violates the required infrastructure tagging policies.

Expected Outcome

The GitHub Actions workflow provides an alternative to the existing Jenkins governance process by dynamically retrieving IMAC configuration from DynamoDB and enforcing infrastructure tagging policies against Terraform plans.
